<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongol-Oirat Code</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1640">1640</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ikh Tsaaz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongol-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> Code was a law code agreed in 1640 at an assembly of Oirat and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha</a> Mongol princes, at which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdeni-batur">Erdeni Batur</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> played a leading part. Aimed at uniting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> against outside threats, it regulated relations between princes, military duties, crimes and the place of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhism</a>. It remained the basis of law among the Dzungars and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmyks">Kalmyks</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>.</p></div>
